Aim
To simulate Mobile IP in OMNeT++ (INET) and observe the signalling used when a mobile node moves from its home network to a foreign network.
Detailed Algorithm
1.  Open the INET Mobile IPv6 example (the mipv6 example folder) and copy it as MobileIPDemo. The network contains a Mobile Node (MN), a Home Agent (HA), a Correspondent Node (CN), routers and access points for the home and foreign networks.
2.  Configure the MN to move on a path from the home access point to the foreign access point (waypoint or linear mobility).
3.  Run a UDP or ping stream from the CN to the MN's home address.
4.  While at home the MN receives packets directly. When the MN attaches to the foreign network it receives a Router Advertisement (movement detection).
5.  The MN forms a care-of address (CoA) from the foreign prefix.
6.  The MN sends a Binding Update (BU) to the HA; the HA stores the home-address-to-CoA binding and replies with a Binding Acknowledgement (BA).
7.  Packets from the CN to the home address are intercepted by the HA and tunnelled (IP-in-IP) to the CoA.
8.  Optional route optimisation: the Return Routability messages (HoTI, CoTI, HoT, CoT) are exchanged and the MN sends a BU to the CN so that later packets go directly.
9.  Plot the packets received at the MN against time and note the gap during handover; view the sequence chart.
